window.FWN_YOU_PROMISED_TO_BE_AN_IDLE_SON_IN_LAW_HOW_COULD_YOU_BECOME_A_LAND_IMMORTAL_CHAPTERS=(window.FWN_YOU_PROMISED_TO_BE_AN_IDLE_SON_IN_LAW_HOW_COULD_YOU_BECOME_A_LAND_IMMORTAL_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":601,"title":"Chapter 601 - 338: Only Advance, No Retreat","paragraphs":["By the time the Holy Emperor’s decree arrived in Shu State, it was already the twenty-ninth day of the ninth month.","Only one day remained until the Annual Examination.","Tomorrow, the scholars from the Prefecture City and surrounding counties and towns would all gather at the examination grounds—a large courtyard located between the Governor’s Office and the Prefectural Magistrate’s Office.","The examination would last for two days. They would enter at 5:00 AM, the exam would begin at 1:00 PM, and it would end at Noon on the second day.","Originally, Ma Shuhan, the Academic Administrator Officer of Shu State, had scheduled the Annual Examination for the twenty-eighth, but for some unspeakable reason, he had postponed it by two days. The scholars in the Prefecture City were not merely understanding or supportive of this change; they simply had no time to pay attention to it.","The reasons behind Liu Hong’s death had already spread far and wide: colluding with the enemy and betraying the country, manipulating grain prices, attempting to spread a plague, and so on. Each and every one of his crimes was posted on the notice board outside the Governor’s Office.","Listed alongside him were the crimes of those who had been taken away by the Imprisonment Department. Ye Jingxiao, the Vice Inspector General of the Inspectorate Office, had colluded with Lin’s Grain Store to frame loyal officials. Mr. Lingchuan from Guiyun Academy had secretly sold ironware to Poshisu Country on behalf of Commander-in-Chief Zhu Hao. Sun Wutong of the Sun Family had also played his part...","Except for a few individuals who were sentenced to exile, the rest, such as Ye Jingxiao and Zhu Lingchuan, were to be escorted to the Capital Prefecture to await execution after autumn.","As soon as these matters came to light, they caused an uproar throughout Shu State. The commoners cursed them incessantly. Although the soaring grain prices in the Prefecture City had not resulted in mass starvation, the people would never forget the panic of those days. This was true for everyone, whether they had managed to buy grain or not.","\"I originally thought that bastard Liu Hong was a good official, but I didn’t expect him to be so despicable behind the scenes.\"","\"To think I was actually grateful to him for opening the granaries, stabilizing grain prices, and providing disaster relief. Turns out none of that was his true intention.\"","\"Now I finally see clearly. In this Shu State, the only ones who truly treat us commoners well are the Xiao Family.\"","\"If Marquis Xiao hadn’t been unable to stand it anymore and confronted Liu Hong, the grain prices would still be sky-high. Many people would have definitely died back then.\"","\"Don’t forget, it was also Marquis Xiao who discovered the plague first and ordered the Government Office and Physicians to investigate inside and outside the Prefecture City overnight.\"","\"Marquis Xiao and the Xiao Family have protected Shu State for years. We... alas, we truly owe the old man an apology.\"","\"There’s also General Jinghong. The Commander-in-Chief who tried to flee this time was killed by her...\"","The common people on the streets held deep grudges against Liu Hong and the others, and the scholars were no exception. Most likely, the more they thought back on all the things they had done to try and save Mr. Lingchuan, the more ashamed they felt, prompting them to write articles cursing the traitors.","Sayings like \"you may know a person’s face, but not their heart\" were spread countless times. Even a few teachers at Guiyun Academy had voiced their criticisms of Zhu Lingchuan.","However, with the Annual Examination approaching, Mr. Yue Ming, Mr. Zhuo Ying, and others could only try to find ways to force the many scholars to focus. But clearly, it was of little effect.","\"Dean, just let them be.","\"The crimes Liu Gongmo committed this time are truly too massive. Even I want to curse him a few times.\"","Mr. Yue Ming naturally understood this reasoning. He sighed and said, \"Don’t you join in and add to the chaos.\"","Mr. Zhuo Ying raised an eyebrow. \"Adding to the chaos? Isn’t there enough already right now?","\"Before the Holy Emperor’s decree arrives, the Governor’s Office is completely leaderless. Yang Ye alone is already finding it more than he can handle.","\"The situation at the Inspectorate Office is slightly better, but I heard the Capital Commandery has been deeply affected.","\"Although the commoners over in Guangyuan County haven’t made many moves, those Noble Families have caused quite a few disturbances. They are mostly people in the same boat as Zhu Hao.","\"Salt, tea, water transport, carriages, and so on... the Capital Commandery is raiding one or two large clans almost every day. Some are killed, while others are exiled.\"","At this point, he pointed toward the Xiao Family with feigned mystery and said, \"I heard from people over in Guangyuan that Commander Li is making such moves because of Xiao Jinghong.\"","Mr. Yue Ming frowned slightly. \"Xiao Jinghong?\"","After thinking for a moment, his brow smoothed out. \"It must be that after she killed Zhu Hao last time, she heavily pressured the Capital Commandery.\"","Mr. Zhuo Ying smiled and nodded. \"Although that girl is a woman, she acts decisively and without hesitation. She has a bit of Xiao Fengchun’s flair.","\"On the other hand, Marquis Xiao... Dean, have you heard about the Xiao Family’s recent moves?","\"You should know a bit, seeing as you and Marquis Xiao are considered bosom friends.\"","Hearing this, Mr. Yue Ming glared at him. \"I am not familiar with him!\"","However, he had indeed heard about the Xiao Family’s recent situation. Ever since Liu Hong’s death, people from several families in the Prefecture City had flocked to visit the Xiao Family, all bringing copious amounts of gifts.","Take the Wan Family, for example. Not only did they gift the Xiao Family medicinal ingredients from their Medicine Hall, but they also brought ten thousand silver coins. The other few families did the same. It was as if the previous attacks the Xiao Family had endured from the various Noble Families of Shu State had never happened.","After a moment of silence, Mr. Yue Ming spoke. \"Liu Hong is dead, and the Jing State Liu Family behind him has also fallen. Anyone with a discerning eye can see that this was the work of the Xiao Family.","\"At this time, their visits to the Xiao Family are nothing more than an attempt to mend relations with them.\"","Mr. Zhuo Ying sneered. \"A bunch of fence-sitters. Since they weren’t implicated by Liu Hong, they will sooner or later be settled by Marquis Xiao.\" He toyed with the teacup in his hand and changed the subject. \"However, with Qingzhou not coming to the academy these past few days, I’m still a bit unaccustomed to it.\"","\"With the Annual Examination approaching, it’s normal for Qingzhou to study harder,\" Mr. Yue Ming said.","\"With Qingzhou’s knowledge, if he can’t make it into the top three of the Annual Examination, who else could?\"","\"Hard to say.\" Mr. Yue Ming thought of the Academic Administrator Officer who hadn’t been affected by Liu Hong, and said with a slight sigh, \"If Ma Shuhan doesn’t play any tricks, even if Qingzhou doesn’t make the top three, he will still rank among the best. I’m just afraid that Ma Shuhan won’t act according to common sense.\"","Mr. Zhuo Ying snorted. \"Would he dare?","\"Previously, he had Liu Hong backing him up. Now that Liu Hong is dead and the Governor’s Office is controlled by Lord Yang, how could he still be allowed to act recklessly?\""]},{"number":602,"title":"Chapter 602 - 338: Only Advance, No Retreat","paragraphs":["\"I hope so...\"","Just as Mr. Yue Ming was agonizing over how to pacify the academy students and get them to focus on preparing for the Annual Examination, the sound of footsteps came from outside the door.","Ma Guan’s figure appeared shortly after. He panted, \"De-Dean, Mr. Zhuo Ying, the Holy Emperor’s decree has arrived in Shu State.\"","\"Quick, tell us.\"","\"Eunuch Feng, the Chief Eunuch who arrived a few days ago, went to the Governor’s Office first.\" Ma Guan caught his breath, calmed down, and said, \"Lord Yang is temporarily acting as the Governor.\"","Mr. Yue Ming and Mr. Zhuo Ying exchanged a glance, visible relief washing over their faces.","\"Dean, with Elder Yang overseeing the Governor’s Office, the Annual Examination should proceed much more smoothly.\"","Mr. Yue Ming nodded slightly. \"If Ma Shuhan dares to act arbitrarily, I will naturally go and reason with him.\"","He had previously approached Yang Ye when Ma Shuhan invited him to serve as a deputy examiner; their personal relationship was decent. He then looked at Ma Guan. \"Where did Eunuch Feng go after leaving the Governor’s Office?\"","Ma Guan shook his head. \"Dean, Eunuch Feng is still at the Governor’s Office at this moment.\"","\"Oh?\"","\"Aside from Lord Yang, another person at the Governor’s Office received a reward from the Holy Emperor. It is the Golden Imperial Top Scholar, Chen Yunfan.","\"It’s said that he discovered Commander Zhu Hao’s iron trade with Poshisu Country and handed the evidence of his crimes to Inspector General Tang Zixing.","\"There’s also Lv Jiunan...\" Ma Guan said with a strange expression. \"For some unknown reason, the Holy Emperor’s decree stated that Assistant Governor Chen killed Lv Jiunan.\"","Mr. Yue Ming naturally had heard of Lv Jiunan’s name. He recalled, \"If I remember correctly, rumor has it that Lv Jiunan was killed by ’Dragon Tiger’ Liu Wu.\" He looked at Mr. Zhuo Ying. \"Is that right?\"","Mr. Zhuo Ying nodded and pondered for a moment. \"Could it be that Chen Yunfan is actually the famous Liu Wu of Shu State?\"","\"Him?\"","\"It is somewhat possible...\"","What absolute nonsense!","Chen Yunfan, currently at the Governor’s Office, truly couldn’t clear his name even if he had a hundred mouths.","Previously, he only thought that claiming credit with Lv Jiunan’s corpse would earn him Chen Yi’s mockery, but he had forgotten another crucial detail.","\"Dragon Tiger\" Liu Wu was hidden too deeply!","Now, not only did outsiders suspect he was Liu Wu, but even people inside the Governor’s Office shared the same thought. Li Huai’gu was one of them.","After Feng Erbao and the others left the Governor’s Office to head to the Xiao Family, Li Huai’gu came knocking. He looked Chen Yunfan up and down, cupped his fists, and said, \"Pardon my disrespect. I never expected Lord Assistant Governor to possess such profound Martial Arts.\"","Chen Yunfan rolled his eyes and tossed aside the imperial decree in his hand. \"Get lost, get lost... Stop bringing up things I don’t want to hear.","\"Anyone with eyes can see that this Assistant Governor couldn’t possibly be that ’Dragon Tiger’. Only idiots would think otherwise.\"","Li Huai’gu smiled and asked, \"Then why did the imperial decree state that you killed Lv Jiunan?\"","\"I...\" Chen Yunfan leaned back in his chair, waving his hand weakly. \"Forget it, forget it. Just treat me as that dog-fart Liu Wu.\"","He couldn’t exactly admit that he had merely picked up Lv Jiunan’s corpse. Saying that wouldn’t just strip him of all dignity; even the Holy Emperor would have to punish him for the crime of deceiving the sovereign.","Seeing this, Li Huai’gu sat down opposite him. He could mostly tell that there was a hidden story behind all this. After thinking for a moment, a hint of confusion appeared on his face. \"Logically speaking, since Brother Yunfan achieved such a great merit, the reward should have been much larger.\"","\"Larger?\" Chen Yunfan said grumpily. \"Brother Huai’gu, do you want the Holy Emperor to confer me the title of Right Minister of the Governor’s Office right now? Or take over Zhu Hao’s vacancy?\"","Despite his words, he was also somewhat puzzled.","Previously, when Chen Yi handed Zhu Hao’s criminal evidence to him on behalf of the White Tiger Guard, he thought that merit would allow him to take another step forward. Even if he didn’t skip a grade to reach the Junior Third Grade, he should have at least reached the Senior Fourth Grade.","But the truth was, he only received a few words of praise from the Holy Emperor, along with some gold, silver, and jewels.","After chatting for a few more sentences, Li Huai’gu got up and left.","Chen Yunfan sat quietly in his chair, looking out the window at the bright sun with a complex expression on his face. \"Now I don’t even know how Brother Yi is going to mock me...\"","Damn it, this was all Lin Zhong’s fault for being a busybody.","...","The Xiao Family.","Inside Spring Lotus Garden.","Chen Yi had naturally heard about the events at the Governor’s Office, as well as the fact that Chen Yunfan took credit for Lv Jiunan’s corpse. He figured it must have been the doing of Lin Zhong, the Chen Family’s Guard Commander.","This was fine, too. Lv Jiunan’s corpse keeping space here was bound to turn into dirt anyway; he might as well use it to give Chen Yunfan some achievements.","Moreover, there was an unexpected bonus—the people of Shu State deducing that Chen Yunfan was \"Dragon Tiger\" Liu Wu fit perfectly with Chen Yi’s wishes. Previously, he had used his illness from the plague poison to completely clear his own name. Now, with this incident involving Chen Yunfan, he guessed that no one would associate \"Liu Wu\" with him anymore.","Laughing it off, Chen Yi shifted his attention to the Qingjing Residence in the middle courtyard.","\"...Your merits and faults balance out, and you are fined three years of your salary. Respect this!\"","\"Xiao Yuan thanks the Holy Emperor for his grace.\"","\"Marquis Xiao, the Holy Emperor also asked me to pass a message to you.\"","\"Please speak, Eunuch Feng.\"","\"The Holy Emperor said that from now on, you can only advance and never retreat; otherwise, if chaos erupts in Shu State, you alone will be held responsible.\"","\"Please help me thank the Holy Emperor, Eunuch...\"","Hearing this, Chen Yi circulated the Black Tortoise Concealment Technique, drawing in his aura to prevent any leakage. He flipped through the ancient text in his hand, a smile curving his lips.","It was exactly as he had thought.","The current Holy Emperor didn’t reprimand the Old Master too harshly, merely fining him some salary to gloss over the matter. However, that oral decree was rather interesting.","He thought, \"The current Holy Emperor’s gaze must have been on Shu State this whole time. He is well aware of the Old Master’s recent actions.","\"Instead, the Old Master has become somewhat like a frightened bird, putting all his effort into restoring the Xiao Family’s prestige.\"","This wasn’t hard to deduce.","If the current Holy Emperor had wanted to use thunderous methods against the Xiao Family, he wouldn’t have let him and Chen Yunfan come to Shu State. He wouldn’t have done it before, and now that the Xiao Family’s situation was improving, he certainly wouldn’t do it now.","He estimated that...","The chessboard in Chen Yi’s mind shifted slightly. Several chess pieces hopped around, and as the game changed, his brows furrowed slightly.","\"Chen Yunfan has enough merit on his end, only lacking some seniority. Once the new year passes, the Capital Prefecture will issue a new decree for him,\" he analyzed. \"So... am I next?\"","Right now, the chessboard of Shu State was already gaining momentum, at least for Chen Yunfan. If Chen Yi was the Chess Master who laid out the plans, he would definitely push the board simultaneously to reach the endgame. In other words, this \"Fledgling\" had to accomplish something within the Xiao Family.","\"It seems this son-in-law will also have to make a move after the Annual Examination,\" he pondered.","Chen Yi thought about getting up to stretch his muscles. Just as he was about to tidy up the study, a shout came from outside the courtyard.","\"Brother-in-law, I’m back, brother-in-law...\"","Following closely were fits of RING RING RING sounds.","Chen Yi looked towards the sound and saw Pei Guanli bouncing and skipping her way over. Her tender white bare feet stepped on the bluestone slabs without leaving a single footprint, and the large bell on her chest bobbed up and down, swaying back and forth.","She first saw Xiaodie sweeping outside the wooden building and chuckled, \"Sister Xiaodie, where is my brother-in-law?\"","Xiaodie responded and smiled, \"The young master is in the study reading. The Annual Examination is tomorrow, don’t you...\"","Don’t you what? She couldn’t even finish her sentence.","Pei Guanli bypassed her and headed straight for the study, shouting for her brother-in-law.","Xiaodie scrambled to keep up behind her. \"Miss Pei, you, you shouldn’t disturb the young master’s reading.\"","\"It’s fine, it won’t get in the way. I’m just looking for...\" As Pei Guanli spoke, she arrived at the study. With one glance, she spotted Chen Yi standing at the desk, and a look of joy couldn’t help but appear on her face. \"Brother-in-law! I’m back!\"","Pei Guanli kicked off the ground and flew forward.","Chen Yi looked helpless. He calmly stepped sideways to dodge, grabbed her with a clever technique, and said, \"I’m not deaf, nor am I blind.\"","Pei Guanli held his hand and giggled, her eyes filled entirely with his reflection. But after laughing for a bit, she then pouted and grumbled, \"You say that, but brother-in-law promised me before that you’d pick me up once you were done with your work. In the end, I waited a long time and didn’t see you come.\"","Chen Yi signaled for Xiaodie to prepare lunch while casting a sidelong glance at Pei Guanli. \"How come I heard that you were in closed-door Cultivation?\"","Pei Guanli rolled her eyes twice, her lips curling up naturally. She pulled him and stammered, \"It’s all Third Granduncle’s fault. He insisted on teaching me some Witchcraft and Gu Skill, hehe...\"","Seeing Xiaodie walk far away, Chen Yi brushed Pei Guanli aside, sat down on a chair, and asked with a smile, \"Did your brother and the others go back?\"","Pei Guanli leaned against his side, tilted her face up to look at him, and nodded. \"Ah Ma sent a letter telling them to return.\"","\"So urgently? Did something happen with the Mountain Race?\"","\"Not in the tribe. Brother said that the Wu Mountain Mutual Market is about to be completed, so Ah Ma asked him to go back and prepare mountain goods.\"","Chen Yi realized. Before Xiao Jinghong left, she had mentioned the matter of the Mutual Market; now, it was finally nearing completion. This could be considered one of the few pieces of good news for the Xiao Family recently.","Pei Guanli didn’t think about all that. She chirped continuously, chattering about the things she had heard during her closed-door Cultivation.","\"Brother-in-law, did you know that something major is about to happen in the Jianghu?\""]},{"number":603,"title":"Chapter 603 - 339: I Am Also a Fool!","paragraphs":["A major event in the Jianghu.","Chen Yi naturally knew about it. It was nothing more than the duel between Immortal Bai and some swordsman.","\"What’s the matter?\" Chen Yi asked.","Seeing him looking over, Pei Guanli lowered her voice and said, \"Ah Ma said in her letter that Immortal Bai, the most powerful person in the Jianghu, is going to duel someone in the upper reaches of the Chishui River.\"","\"Duel who?\"","\"Monarch Xue Jian, Lone Immortal Ye.\"","Chen Yi raised an eyebrow. \"This person...\"","\"Brother-in-law, you also know Monarch Xue Jian? My brother and Third Granduncle both said he is the most powerful swordsman after Sword Master Li Wudang.\"","\"...Never heard of him.\"","\"He—\" Pei Guanli’s joyful smile faltered. \"You’ve never heard of him, brother-in-law?\"","Chen Yi smiled and nodded. \"I really don’t know him.\"","These past few days, his mind had been focused on solving the Xiao family’s troubles. The Jianghu anecdotes he occasionally heard were only fragmented and incomplete. Like the reclusive Immortal Bai, as well as his disciple Shui Hetong. Xiao Jinghong’s master, Sword Master Li Wudang. Liu Lang’s master, Sword Ghost Chu Xiudao, and the Celestial Sect where Xie Tingyun and Shen Huatang were from. These great seniors of the Jianghu were mostly connected to the people around Chen Yi, so he had heard more about them. As for the other Jianghu People, he naturally had never heard of them and didn’t care much either.","\"Tell me, what’s the background of this Monarch Xue Jian, Lone Immortal Ye?\"","Pei Guanli’s expression immediately brightened. She began to chatter away about Lone Immortal Ye.","She originally didn’t know who Monarch Xue Jian was either. Fortunately, Pei Qian and the others had told her quite a bit before they left.","\"Alone on the snowy peak for nineteen springs,","Plum blossoms fall on shoulders untouched by dust.","Today I draw my sword for you,","Only to realize I, too, am a fool.","\"Monarch Xue Jian was originally a legitimate son of the Ye family in Ji State. He was born with extraordinary talent.","\"It’s said that he started practicing Martial Arts at the age of six, and broke through to the Eighth Grade Realm by eight... Brother-in-law, what are you laughing at?\"","Chen Yi held back his laughter and waved his hand. \"I’m not laughing, I’m not. Go on.\"","Pei Guanli puffed out her cheeks, her round face full of indignation. \"I just had a mishap when practicing Martial Arts, but my Cultivation is also close to the Seventh Grade now.\"","However, thinking of Chen Yi’s current title of \"Dragon Tiger,\" she muttered a few words in resignation, saying things about how Third Granduncle had taught her a lot and that she would sooner or later reach the Middle Three Grades Realm.","Before Chen Yi could offer a few words of comfort, she continued, \"Third Granduncle said that Lone Immortal Ye reached the Sixth Grade at ten, and by fifteen, his Cultivation had already reached the Upper Fourth Grade. He was only one step away from breaking through to the Upper Three Grades Realm.","\"But right at that time...\"","When Lone Immortal Ye was sixteen, the Ye family committed a taboo. Not only did they offend a prominent family in Ji State, but they also accidentally killed a core disciple of the Gouchen Sect, bringing a great disaster upon the Ye family. First, the taverns the family relied on for their livelihood were ransacked. Then, the distant branch members died bizarre deaths one after another. And just as they were discussing whether to fight or seek peace, the people from the Gouchen Sect launched a night attack on their doorstep.","It was the Mid-Autumn Festival. There were exactly one hundred and forty-three people in the Ye family’s ancestral estate. Despite their desperate resistance, under the overwhelming power of the Gouchen Sect Leader, Lone Immortal Ye was the only one in the entire Ye family to escape alive.","\"After that, the Gouchen Sect relentlessly hunted Lone Immortal Ye down...\" Pei Guanli waved her fist, looking indignant herself. \"Fortunately, Lone Immortal Ye was strong enough. Not only did he escape, but he also took less than two years to advance his Cultivation to the First Grade Realm.\"","Chen Yi nodded in understanding. \"And then he successfully took his revenge?\"","Pei Guanli’s small face fell, and she shook her head. \"He only wiped out the entire Gouchen Sect. As for that prominent family, many of their people survived.\"","\"Oh?\"","\"According to my Third Granduncle, Lone Immortal Ye was saved by a woman while he was on the run. By sheer coincidence, she turned out to be the young lady of that very same prominent family.\"","\"So...\" Chen Yi raised an eyebrow. \"So he let that family off?\"","Pei Guanli hummed in agreement and pouted. \"When he went to seek revenge, he finally discovered that the woman belonged to that family, and...\" Shaking Chen Yi’s hand, she added, \"And by that time, they had already developed feelings for each other.\"","\"That family managed to survive thanks to that woman...\"","Chen Yi couldn’t help but laugh, likely finding such a story a bit clichéd.","Who knew Pei Guanli’s eyes would dart around as she asked him with a cheeky grin, \"Brother-in-law, what would you do if you were Lone Immortal Ye?\"","\"Me?\" Chen Yi thought about it seriously and shook his head. \"Me? I don’t know. But of course, it’s impossible for me to ever end up in that kind of situation.\"","Hadn’t he spent so much time on Cultivation just to protect himself and the people around him from harm? Given this, if he still managed to fall into a situation like Lone Immortal Ye’s, he might as well just bang his head against a brick wall.","\"What if... it was someone from the Mountain Race who killed the Chen family?\"","\"The Chen family? Then let them be killed.\"","Pei Guanli froze for a moment. \"Brother-in-law, you wouldn’t avenge the Chen family?\"","Chen Yi smiled and tapped her forehead. \"Because you are in the Mountain Race.\"","Pei Guanli immediately giggled, her face showing a rare blush. \"Brother-in-law, I’d never put you in a tough spot.","\"If anyone from the Mountain Race really is blind enough to cross you, I promise to plant a few Gu Insects in them and make them regret ever being born.\"","\"You’re one to talk,\" Chen Yi said. \"Did you forget about Poisoning Chen Yunfan last time?\"","\"Ah, geez...\"","Amidst the chatter and laughter, by the time Xiaodie came to announce that lunch was ready, Chen Yi had mostly understood what kind of person Lone Immortal Ye was.","After settling his grievances with the Le family—the prominent family in Ji State—Lone Immortal Ye lived a reclusive life, hiding away from the world. He stayed hidden for nineteen years. When he descended the mountain again, his Cultivation had reached the Grandmaster Realm, achieving Sword Dao Perfection. The last time news of Lone Immortal Ye spread was four years ago when he challenged Li Jin, a Grandmaster Realm swordsman in Ji State, and killed him in just ten sword strikes.","Chen Yi ate his lunch while silently calculating in his mind. If Lone Immortal Ye was capable of challenging Immortal Bai, his Cultivation and Sword Dao must have both ascended to a whole new level."]},{"number":604,"title":"Chapter 604 - 339: I Am Also a Fool!","paragraphs":["Either his Cultivation had reached the Great Grandmaster realm, or his Sword Dao had been honed to the Extreme Realm. Otherwise, even if Lone Immortal Ye was willing, Immortal Bai probably wouldn’t bother with him.","\"Great Grandmaster... Sword Dao Ultimate Realm...\"","Martial Arts Cultivation was divided from the Ninth Grade to the First Grade; above that were the realms of Grandmaster and Great Grandmaster. And the Technique Realm consisted of entry-level, Minor Success, Great Success, Perfection, and the Extreme Realm—where Skill Nears the Dao.","Reaching that realm earned one the respectful title of \"Land Immortal,\" meaning they had achieved \"Extreme Mortality.\"","However, even among those in that realm, there were differences in strength. Cultivation, Technique, Cultivation Technique, and talent—even the slightest variations could affect Heaven and Earth’s Spiritual Mechanism. For example, it was said that Immortal Bai had cultivated two Techniques to the Extreme Realm, which was why he was hailed as the number one person in Martial Arts.","At this thought, a smile naturally formed on Chen Yi’s face. He might fall short when it came to the Technique Realm, but in terms of sheer quantity, if he claimed to be second, who would dare claim to be first?","Of course, as long as he was given enough time, he would inevitably catch up.","After lunch, Chen Yi didn’t continue reading; instead, he planned to visit the Jishi Medicine Hall and the Hundred Herbs Hall. Since he had decided to turn from passive to active, he needed to make some preparations.","Seeing him change into a set of clean brocade clothes, Xiaodie couldn’t help but ask, \"Are you going out, Sir?\"","\"Yes. I’ve stayed in the manor for so many days, so I’m going out to stretch my legs.\"","\"B-but tomorrow is the Annual Examination.\"","Chen Yi adjusted his clothes, turned his head to look at her, and smiled. \"Studying requires a balance of tension and relaxation. Being strung too tight isn’t good.\"","Xiaodie nodded, half-understanding. \"I see...\"","Beside them, Pei Guanli started laughing, thinking that her brother-in-law was spouting nonsense again. However, seeing that Chen Yi was heading out, she trotted after him, clamoring that she wanted to go too.","Chen Yi thought for a moment and nodded in agreement. Pei Guanli then giggled and left the Spring Lotus Garden together with him.","Xiaodie watched them walk away, full of envy. Of course, she envied Pei Guanli.","In fact, during these past few days when Chen Yi had devoted all his attention to reading in the study, Xiaodie was the happiest person. Even though Chen Yi rarely needed her to serve him, she felt a sweet satisfaction in her heart and was brimming with energy. Boiling water, sweeping, doing laundry, serving tea, preparing meals, and so on—Xiaodie had grown accustomed to this routine and was used to staying by Chen Yi’s side.","Therefore, she really disliked being alone in the Spring Lotus Garden. Even though she would clean the inside and outside of the garden until it was spotless, she always felt an emptiness in her heart.","Xiaodie stared blankly into the distance for a moment before gathering her emotions. She then ran back to the side room, took out the \"Biography of the Marquis’s Mansion’s Second Son-in-Law,\" and began to write, stroke by stroke.","\"On the twenty-ninth of September in the 21st year of Anhe, Sir was reading in the study during the morning. I ran over to tell him that the Holy Emperor’s decree had arrived...\"","Naturally, Chen Yi was unaware of Xiaodie’s thoughts. He led Pei Guanli all the way through the middle courtyard and arrived at the front courtyard. At this time, Feng Erbao and the others who had come to announce the decree had just left the Xiao Family, and Elder Master Xiao and the rest were returning from the entrance.","Chen Yi ran into them head-on and bowed in greeting. \"Elder Master.\"","Elder Master Xiao’s expression was relatively relaxed, seemingly unaffected by the Holy Emperor’s decree of punishment. He glanced at Pei Guanli before his clear eyes landed on Chen Yi. He nodded with a peaceful expression and asked, \"I heard Qingzhou is going to participate in the Annual Examination tomorrow?\"","Chen Yi caught sight of Xiao Xuanshuo, Xiao Shen, and the others from the corner of his eye and responded with a smile, \"Yes.\"","\"I believe that with your knowledge, the Annual Examination won’t stump you, but don’t drop your guard either.\"","Elder Master Xiao offered a few words of encouragement. He then cheerfully greeted Pei Guanli, asked a bit about the Mountain Race’s recent situation, and led his people back to the Qingjing Residence.","Chen Yi exchanged greetings with the others one by one. Only after watching their figures disappear around the corner did he take Pei Guanli by the hand and walk out of the Marquis’s Mansion.","Pei Guanli asked thoughtfully, \"Brother-in-law, I feel like Grandpa Xiao is a bit different from before.\"","While observing the passing commoners and Wandering Martial Artists along the street, Chen Yi asked casually, \"How so?\"","\"He isn’t coughing as much? I remember when we first came to Shu State, Grandpa Xiao was terribly ill. Now, he looks as if he’s fully recovered. Furthermore...\" Pei Guanli patted her chest, causing her Bell to ring JINGLE JINGLE. \"Xiaohua says Grandpa Xiao is very formidable.\"","Chen Yi replied noncommittally, \"Is that so? Perhaps the Elder Master found a Divine Doctor.\"","\"A Divine Doctor? Brother-in-law, aren’t you...\"","\"Hmm?\"","Pei Guanli almost let the secret slip. She stuck out her tongue and shut her mouth. However, before they had taken more than a few steps, she couldn’t help but ask again, \"Brother-in-law, when do you plan to let Sister Jinghong know?\"","Chen Yi paused his steps for a brief moment before resuming his calm pace forward. \"She’ll know when it’s time for her to know.\"","\"When is that?\"","\"Take a guess...\"","Now that Liu Hong was dead, along with the vast majority of those harboring malicious intentions, the crisis facing the Xiao Family was temporarily resolved. Yet, Chen Yi still hadn’t considered revealing everything to Xiao Jinghong.","Originally, he had worried that the \"Fledgling\" identity forced onto him by the White Tiger Guard would make Xiao Jinghong suspect him of plotting against the Xiao Family. But after experiencing so many things, he suddenly realized that hiding a few secrets carried quite a few benefits.","For one, outsiders targeting the Xiao Family would largely ignore a scholar like him, at most assuming he was a frail intellectual with decent handwriting. Secondly, the Xiao Family had too few hidden trump cards, leaving them completely exposed and easily seen through by others. However, with him acting from the shadows, anyone wanting to target the Xiao Family would have to think twice.","At the very least, he needed to wait until he had cleared everything up and laid low for a while before saying anything.","***","Meanwhile, inside the Qingjing Residence.","Elder Master Xiao gave Xiao Xuanshuo, Xiao Shen, and the others a few instructions before dismissing them. The Holy Emperor’s punishment had not exceeded his expectations. But he hadn’t anticipated that the Holy Emperor would let them off so lightly this time, merely deducting three years of salary and letting the matter drop.","This actually made him somewhat worried.","After pondering for a moment, Elder Master Xiao looked towards a corner and said in a deep voice, \"Send an eagle message to Jinghong. Tell her that Feng Erbao has already visited, everything in the manor is normal, and she should focus on inspecting the troops in the Three Towns.\"","Xiao Jing agreed in a low voice. Just as he was about to leave, he heard the Elder Master continue, \"And also Chen Qingzhou...\" He hesitated for a moment before saying, \"Tell Jinghong that Qingzhou is going to take his Annual Examination tomorrow.\"","Xiao Jing agreed once more, though he inwardly disapproved. He thought that a trivial matter like the Annual Examination shouldn’t be reported to Xiao Jinghong at this time, lest it distract her.","Elder Master Xiao naturally paid no mind to Xiao Jing’s thoughts. He remained silent for a moment before ordering, \"Recently, many Wandering Martial Artists have been appearing in Shu State City. To prevent any Evil Demonic Dao among them from causing trouble, send a few people to follow Qingzhou...\" Before he could finish, he realized it was inappropriate and waved it off. \"Forget it. You go personally.\"","Xiao Jing revealed his figure in confusion. \"Marquis, you want me to protect the second son-in-law?\"","\"Protect?\" A somewhat complicated expression appeared on Elder Master Xiao’s face. \"It would be great if you could actually protect him. I’m just afraid...\" He paused mid-sentence and waved his hand. \"Just do as I say, and remember not to draw any attention.\"","Xiao Jing nodded. \"Understood.\"","Unexpectedly, Elder Master Xiao followed up with a reminder: \"Also, remember not to get too close to him. Keep a distance of at least five miles.\"","Xiao Jing was stunned and looked at him in bewilderment. \"This...\"","\"Just do it!\"","\"Yes, sir...\"","After the utterly baffled Xiao Jing left, Elder Master Xiao looked at the teacup on the table and sighed softly.","These past few days, he had been secretly investigating, mostly focusing on what Chen Yi had done and where he had gone since arriving in Shu State. Despite all his searching, he still couldn’t bring himself to believe that Chen Yi was the \"Dragon Tiger\" Liu Wu.","Although there were a few clues—such as Wang Ji practically being driven out of the Xiao Family by Chen Yi’s own hands, Chen Yi frequently visiting the Hundred Herbs Hall, or the fact that he, Chen Yu, and Liu Wu had never appeared at the same time—these were only speculations. They couldn’t definitively prove that Chen Yi was Chen Yu, or that he was the \"Dragon Tiger\" Liu Wu.","No matter how unparalleled a person’s talent was, it was impossible for them to achieve greatness across the Martial Arts, Medical Dao, and Calligraphy Dao all at once, right? Not to mention, with Chen Yu managing the Hundred Herbs Hall, Liu Wu secretly assisting the Xiao Family, and Chen Yi working as an Instructor at Guiyun Academy... he would be stretched too thin, wouldn’t he?","Elder Master Xiao rubbed his brow and thought, \"If I still don’t find anything, I’ll just have to make a move personally...\""]},{"number":605,"title":"Chapter 605 - 340: Truly a Peerless Talent","paragraphs":["Although Elder Master Xiao didn’t believe Liu Hong’s nonsense, the matter involved the internal affairs of the Xiao Family, so he had to investigate it thoroughly. This would prevent him from making any misjudgments in the future.","Just as he was thinking about this, his ears twitched slightly. A familiar voice rang out from outside the front gates.","\"Go report immediately! Tell that old thief Xiao Yuan to prepare some good wine and food. I’ve been starving for a decent meal on this damn journey!\"","\"Lord... Lord Duke? Quick, please come in first. I’ll go inform the master right away.\"","\"Come in? The main gates aren’t even open, and that old bastard Xiao hasn’t come out to greet me. What kind of manners is it for me to just walk in like this? I traveled all this way to bail your master out of trouble, so shouldn’t he come out to welcome me personally?\"","\"Yes, right away...\"","Lu Guan, who was guarding the gates, didn’t dare delay and ran inside in a panic. Hearing Duke Qian Zhang Xuan’s shameless remarks, a smile bloomed on Elder Master Xiao’s face, dispelling the annoyance caused by the Holy Emperor’s recent punishment. Before Lu Guan could reach him, he leaned on his cane and walked out of the Qingjing Residence, instructing the Personal Guard Armored Warriors along the way to prepare their finest wines and rarest delicacies.","Spotting him from a distance, Lu Guan stopped and bowed. Only when Elder Master Xiao drew near did he whisper, \"Master, Lord Duke Qian is at the gates. There are two others accompanying him...\"","Elder Master Xiao gave a hum of acknowledgment. Leaning on his cane, he strode swiftly out of the mansion gates and saw Zhang Xuan standing with his hands behind his back, facing away from him.","\"Old fool, what do you see staring up at the sky like that? Is it going to be windy or rainy tomorrow?\"","Hearing Elder Master Xiao’s teasing, Zhang Xuan turned his head. \"It’s going to hail and crush you to death, you old bastard.","\"I traveled countless miles, personally bringing men to deliver food and silver coins to you, and this is how you treat your benefactor?\"","Elder Master Xiao looked him up and down. Seeing his slightly haggard complexion, he felt a sense of gratitude and comfort, but his words remained unforgiving. \"During the great battle five years ago, when Left King Mu Hage charged the lines, you almost died under his Heavy Mace. Who blocked it for you?","\"And twenty years ago, who led three thousand soldiers of the Profound Armor Army to arrive just in time to save you?\"","Seeing him bringing up the past again, Zhang Xuan waved his hand repeatedly. \"Alright, alright! That was years ago, why even bring it up?\" He pointed at the gates of the Marquis’s Mansion. \"Is this your way of treating guests?\"","Knowing Zhang Xuan was acting shamelessly just to find a way out of the argument, Elder Master Xiao waved his hand, signaling Lu Guan to open the main gates. \"Let’s go drink.\"","\"That’s more like it.\"","Zhang Xuan walked past Elder Master Xiao with his head held high, not forgetting to instruct the two men behind him, \"Wait outside the city. I’ll have someone notify you later about where to deliver the grain.\"","\"Yes, Lord Duke.\" The two middle-aged men, dressed in green robes with long blades hanging from their waists, cupped their hands in a salute before turning and riding away.","Elder Master Xiao glanced at the two men and caught up with Zhang Xuan. \"Their Cultivation is not weak.\"","Zhang Xuan kept his head held high and said proudly, \"Of course the experts my son found aren’t weak. Did you think everyone is like you, guarding against Jianghu People like they’re thieves?\"","Elder Master Xiao ignored the tease and asked thoughtfully, \"You weren’t this cautious the last time you visited... Did something happen?\"","Zhang Xuan paused, his chin lowering as his expression darkened. \"Those people have been getting more and more rampant lately.\"","\"Who? Those bandits on the eastern sea?\"","\"Who else would dare to pillage my Guangyue Prefecture? If it weren’t for a traitor inside tipping them off, I would have led my troops to wipe them out long ago!\"","Elder Master Xiao frowned slightly. \"Treason?\"","Zhang Xuan snorted. \"Just a bunch of greedy opportunists. Unrefined scum.\"","\"If they’re truly just unrefined scum, why did you bring two experts along?\"","\"You... My son is filial and worried about his old man. Is that a crime?\"","Seeing Zhang Xuan being stubborn to the bitter end, Elder Master Xiao shook his head. \"Traitors from within are more dangerous than enemies from without. It’s good to take precautions.\"","Zhang Xuan waved a hand dismissively. \"Let’s not talk about such depressing matters. I heard you killed Liu Gongmo and were punished by a decree from the Holy Emperor. Tell me, did Liu Gongmo really commit those heinous acts?\"","Elder Master Xiao nodded slightly. \"More than that. He colluded deeply with both the Barbarian Race and the Poshisu Country.\" He paused, his expression turning sorrowful. \"Fengchun’s whereabouts were discovered by the Barbarian Race because he secretly tipped them off.\"","\"Him?!\" Zhang Xuan immediately cursed him as a dog. \"To think Fengchun once saved his life! How dare he bite the hand that fed him?","\"That scum, that bastard, that ungrateful wretch... Old Xiao, you really shouldn’t have let him die so easily. People like him deserve death by a thousand cuts!","\"Why did you kill him so early, and even get yourself punished by the Holy Emperor? You let that dog off too easily!\"","Elder Master Xiao smiled bitterly and shook his head, offering no response.","If Liu Hong hadn’t been dead set on seeking his own demise by bringing up Fu Wanqing, Elder Master Xiao wouldn’t have killed him, no matter how furious he was. But thinking about it now, it was better that he had. If Liu Hong had gone to the Capital Prefecture alive and revealed that Fu Wanqing was among the Barbarian Race, the consequences would have been far more unacceptable. Elder Master Xiao didn’t dare to imagine how Xiao Jinghong would react if he found out.","Unaware of all this, Zhang Xuan cursed for a while before pulling him along, declaring that they wouldn’t stop drinking until they were thoroughly drunk tonight. Naturally, Elder Master Xiao didn’t object.","As soon as they took their seats, Zhang Xuan looked at him, the anger freezing on his face. He pointed at him and asked, \"Wait, Old Xiao, you... your health... are you cured?\"","As he instructed the servants to bring the wine and food, Elder Master Xiao smiled and nodded. \"I’m doing a bit better.\"","\"Just a bit better? Looking at your physique, I’d say your old injuries are completely healed!\" Seeing his friend smile without saying a word, Zhang Xuan’s face darkened. \"You’re still hiding things from me? Tell me, who has such incredible ability?\"","\"It’s...\"","Elder Master Xiao thought of Chen Yu and Liu Wu, and then Chen Yi’s face surfaced in his mind. The words reached the tip of his tongue, but he swallowed them back, merely shaking his head as he said..."]},{"number":606,"title":"Chapter 606 - 340: Truly a Peerless Talent","paragraphs":["\"An expert whose movements are as elusive as a divine dragon.\"","Zhang Xuan saw that Elder Master Xiao didn’t want to elaborate. Grumbling a few words, he lifted the wine jar and poured for them both. \"Since that’s the case, I’ll definitely show you my prowess today.\"","Elder Master Xiao put on a smile again. Without another word, he lifted his bowl and downed it in one gulp.","After three rounds of wine, the two began to discuss their respective experiences during this period.","Zhang Xuan had a rough idea of the Xiao Family’s situation in Shu State, particularly the burning of the summer grain in the Three Towns, the soaring grain prices, the refugees, and the plague. However, he didn’t know the exact details. After listening to Elder Master Xiao’s account, he couldn’t help but curse Liu Hong a few more times, repeatedly saying that he was killed too early.","The Elder Master simply laughed it off. Remembering something, he asked, \"How is my second brother doing after arriving in Guangyue Prefecture?\"","Due to Xiao Dongchen’s incident, the second branch of the Xiao Family felt too ashamed to stay in Shu State, so they all went to Guangyue Prefecture to seek refuge with Xiao Qiuyun.","Seeing him mention Xiao Wang, a trace of displeasure surfaced on Zhang Xuan’s face. \"Don’t you know what your own brother is like?","\"Hmph, before he even arrived in Guangyue Prefecture, Qiuyun had already arranged a residence and even begged Ying’er to secure a position for her father.","\"At first, things were fine, and Xiao Wang was relatively well-behaved.","\"But the good times didn’t last. Not even half a month later, he went to Qiuyun saying he wanted to run a Medicine Hall business. He invested a large sum of money from start to finish, but it didn’t even make a splash.","\"And there’s more...\"","Zhang Xuan poured out a torrent of grievances. Finally, he said, \"No wonder you kicked him out of Shu State. If it were me, I wouldn’t have been soft-hearted either.\"","After listening, Elder Master Xiao remained silent for a moment before sighing. \"You can’t write two ’Xiao’ characters with one stroke. In the end, they are all still the Xiao family.\" Immediately after, he changed the subject. \"However much silver coins Qiuyun took from Zhang Ying, and however many connections she used, I will repay you all at once later.\"","Zhang Xuan snorted and said bluntly, \"Can you even afford it?\"","\"It’s just money. I have plenty of ways.\"","\"Boasting like that, aren’t you afraid of losing a few of your Da Ya...\"","The reason Elder Master Xiao was confident in repaying the silver was entirely due to the Wu Mountain Mutual Market and the Hundred Herbs Hall. The former was about to be completed, and merchants from the Mountain Race and neighboring State Capitals had already come to sign contracts with the Xiao Family. In the future, the silver coins naturally wouldn’t be lacking.","The same went for the latter. The Hundred Herbs Hall’s storefront business in Guangyuan County was booming. Just last night, the Fu Family over there had even sent a letter, entirely filled with gratitude for the Xiao Family’s assistance.","After getting a general understanding, Zhang Xuan felt a bit jealous and said, \"You bastard, you have pretty good luck...\"","\"Good luck?\" Thinking of the dire straits he had faced while struggling to maintain the Xiao Family for the past five years, Elder Master Xiao sighed. He picked up his bowl and said, \"Let’s not talk about it anymore. Come, let’s drink.\"","\"Drink, then...\"","The arrival of Zhang Xuan in the middle courtyard slightly dispelled the gloom, and the Armored Warriors and servants began bustling about.","In the backyard, Xiao Wan’er breathed a sigh of relief upon hearing the news.","She thought, \"With Duke Zhang here, Grandpa should be fine.\"","She naturally knew that the Elder Master didn’t have many close friends, especially in Shu State. At a time like this, the only people who could speak a few words with him—aside from her, Xiao Jinghong, and Xiao Wuge—were Duke Qian, Zhang Xuan, and Sun Fu, who had gone to Jinling.","Thinking of this, Xiao Wan’er glanced in the direction of the Spring Lotus Garden. Knowing that Chen Yi had left the Marquis’s Mansion, she instructed Cui’er, \"Have the kitchen prepare a few more light dishes tonight, and also make some pastries for the young master to take with him during his Annual Examination.\"","\"Yes...\"","Chen Yi was naturally unaware of the lively atmosphere inside the Marquis’s Mansion. Leading Pei Guanli, he bypassed the Governor’s Office and the Prefectural Magistrate’s Office, making his way all the way to the East Market.","Along the way, he naturally heard and saw quite a few things.","For instance, on the notice board in front of the Governor’s Office, the names of Liu Hong and others had been smeared with red cinnabar by meddlesome onlookers. At the Prefectural Magistrate’s Office, people were constantly being interrogated, mostly Zhu Lingchuan, Ye Jingxiao, and their ilk, while many commoners gathered in front, clapping, cheering, and clamoring that they all deserved to die. Moreover, some Jianghu People who had just arrived in Shu State were in the taverns, finding locals to ask about the recent situation here—asking if anyone had seen Immortal Bai, or who \"Dragon Tiger\" Liu Wu was, or gossiping about a certain rising star also coming to Shu State, and so on.","Chen Yi couldn’t muster much interest in most of it. The only place he stopped to look at for a moment was the Xinglin Hall, not far from the East Market.","Because three generations of the Jing State Liu Family had been exterminated by a single edict from the Holy Emperor, some of the people in the Xinglin Hall naturally hadn’t been spared either. Aside from Liu Zhaoxue, the other members of the Liu Family had all been arrested and thrown into prison by the Government Office. In a few days, they would be escorted together to the Capital Prefecture. As a result, the Xinglin Hall had also been sealed off by the Government Office. Even the signboard bearing the Minor Achievement Calligraphy Dao inscription had been taken down, its whereabouts unknown.","Pei Guanli followed his gaze. Her smiling face instantly vanished as she snorted and said, \"Third Granduncle and my brother didn’t even tell me when they came to seek revenge against the Five Poison Sect. They made me miss out on all the fun.\"","Chen Yi couldn’t help but laugh. Shaking his head, he said, \"Why would you tag along for something so dangerous?\"","\"Brother-in-law, even you are saying that... Just wait, I’ll go into secluded Cultivation for the next few days. I’ll break through to the Seventh Grade in no time. Isn’t that right, Little Flower?\"","Not only were Pei Guanli’s moods written all over her face, but they also came and went as quickly as the wind. After taking just two steps, she had completely forgotten her previous displeasure, dragging Chen Yi over to join the crowds watching the craftsmen and street performers. Breaking large stones on the chest, molten iron fireworks, and acrobatics—she watched them all one by one. She somehow managed to spend half an hour walking a distance of merely a hundred rods.","Chen Yi wasn’t in a hurry. As he watched the lively performances, he listened to the chatter around him.","\"...Hua Huixiang from Wudang Mountain has reportedly already arrived in Shu State. He’s currently over in Guang’an County.\"","\"Even he came?\"","\"It seems something major is truly happening in the Shu State Jianghu this time...\"","\"Now that several grain merchants have been sealed by the Government Office, the grain supply is still tight. Fortunately, someone stepped in to fill the gap, and the grain prices have become a bit cheaper.\"","\"With Lord Yang from the Governor’s Office keeping watch, who would dare to act recklessly?\"","\"Of course, Lord Yang isn’t a vile villain like Liu Hong...\"","Chen Yi looked at the commoners, feeling a faint sense of emotion in his heart. A while ago, when grain prices were soaring, these people were all full of complaints, without a single smile on their faces. Now that things had stabilized, the atmosphere was indeed entirely different.","No wonder a Saint in this world had once said, ’The Dao of governing a state must begin with enriching the people. When the people are wealthy, they are easily governed; when the people are poor, they are difficult to govern.’ Only when these commoners had silver coins could they settle in their hometowns, cherish their families, respect their superiors, and fear committing crimes. Naturally, they would be easier to govern.","Not long after, Chen Yi brought Pei Guanli to the Jishi Medicine Hall. Seeing the bustling scene inside the hall once again, he called Liu Quan over to ask about their recent situation.","\"Shopkeeper, ever since the Old Marquis killed Liu Hong and the Government Office sealed the Xinglin Hall, things have improved a lot on our side,\" Liu Quan reported. \"Doctor Ma, Elder Li, and the others are so busy every day that their feet barely touch the ground. It’s just that the supply of medicinal herbs is a bit lacking...\"","Remembering that he had previously asked Wang Ji to send someone to contact the Mountain Race, Chen Yi nodded and said, \"Hold on for the time being. The medicinal herbs should arrive in a few days.\"","With the fall of the Xinglin Hall, the original medicinal herb merchants were naturally looking for a way out. People had already approached the Xiao Family, the Wan Family, and the Hundred Herbs Hall. He estimated that in a few more days, none of the Medicine Halls would lack medicinal herbs.","However, Chen Yi didn’t plan to collaborate with those few medicinal herb merchants in Shu State forever. Moving forward, as the Hundred Herbs Hall expanded throughout Shu State and even into the lands of the other Nine State and Three Prefectures, a massive amount of medicinal herbs would be required. It was impossible for him to entrust the supply of medicinal herbs to those opportunistic merchants who only went whichever way the wind blew.","As Chen Yi spoke, he looked at Pei Guanli, who was holding a tea drink and slurping it down—SLURP, SLURP. He said, \"Later, write a letter to your brother. Tell him that someone wants to purchase some medicinal herbs from the Mountain Race in the coming days, and ask him to take good care of the matter.\"","Hearing this, Pei Guanli chuckled. \"Don’t worry, brother-in-law. My brother will definitely get it done for you. If he doesn’t, I won’t let him off the hook.\"","\"We’ll need a large quantity of medicinal herbs. Make sure to emphasize that when you write the letter.\"","\"A large quantity?\" Pei Guanli put down her tea and thought for a moment before saying, \"Then I’d better reach out to Ah Ma. Everyone in the tribe listens to Ah Ma. Whatever amount of medicinal herbs my brother-in-law wants, we’ll have it.\"","Chen Yi raised an eyebrow slightly. He was just about to decline when Pei Guanli continued, \"Don’t worry, don’t worry, leave it to me! If Ah Ma knows it’s for my brother-in-law’s Medicine Hall, she will definitely agree.\"","\"Then I’ll have to trouble you.\"","\"Hehe...\"","Chen Yi asked Liu Quan for a few more details, then shifted his attention to the Physicians. More accurately, he focused on Yuan Liu’er, who was following Ma Liangcai around.","Despite Yuan Liu’er only having been exposed to the Medical Dao for a short time, she was currently already able to assist Ma Liangcai in diagnosing and treating patients. Taking pulses, questioning patients, and observing symptoms—she did all of it with a proper flair. Even the prescriptions she wrote were considered quite accurate.","He thought, \"As expected of someone with peerless innate talent. This speed of progress—TSK TSK...","\"It seems it’s also time to teach her Martial Arts.\""]},{"number":607,"title":"Chapter 607 - 341: Junior Chen Yi Pays His Respects...","paragraphs":["Yuan Liu’er’s Martial Arts talent was even more outstanding than her Medical Dao. With her Innate Twelve Main Meridians unblocked, she would not encounter any bottlenecks in the Ninth Grade, Eighth Grade, or even Seventh Grade.","The subsequent Middle Three Grades Realm focused on cultivating \"God.\" With her foundation in the Medical Dao, this shouldn’t be a major issue either. In other words, as long as Yuan Liu’er followed the step-by-step Cultivation process, breaking through to the Upper Three Grades Realm was only a matter of time.","Sooner or later.","As for Techniques...","Chen Yi looked Yuan Liu’er up and down. A faint glow flashed in his eyes as he used the Qi Observation Skill to inspect her muscles, bones, and overall physique.","He thought, \"Women don’t primarily rely on raw strength; she should take a path of agility and dexterity.","\"The Mountain Shattering Fist, Dragon-slaying Spear, and Brocade Spring Saber Technique all follow a fierce and forceful path. They aren’t suitable for her.","\"Then...\"","Chen Yi glanced at Pei Guanli beside him and immediately knew which Techniques he should teach Yuan Liu’er.","He mused, \"For Pile Skills, I’ll focus on the Big Spear Pile Skill. Once her Cultivation reaches the Eighth Grade, I will pass on the Four Symbols Skill for her Inner Strength.","\"As for Techniques, she needs one for unarmed combat and one for weapons. The former will be the Hundred Flowers Palm. For the latter, Sword Dao is the only viable option left, and the Celestial Flower Flying Sword Technique isn’t a bad choice.\"","Additionally, for Step Techniques, Wandering Dragon and Phoenix would be much more suitable than the Meteor Butterfly Step. As these thoughts raced through his mind, Chen Yi had already finalized the Martial Arts Techniques and skills he would pass down to Yuan Liu’er.","Pei Guanli noticed his gaze and broke into a bright smile. \"Chen Yi, what are you looking at?\"","Chen Yi naturally withdrew his gaze and looked at Yuan Liu’er again. After a moment of thought, he said, \"I haven’t told you yet, but I’ve taken in a disciple.\"","Pei Guanli gasped softly. \"Chen Yi, you have a disciple now?\"","Chen Yi nodded. \"That’s why I need your help with something. I’ll be participating in the Annual Examination for the next two days, so I’d like to ask you to teach my disciple the Big Spear Pile Skill.\"","\"A Pile Skill? That’s easy.\" Pei Guanli patted her chest in assurance, then looked around curiously. \"Chen Yi, you haven’t told me who your disciple is yet. Who’s the lucky guy?\"","Chen Yi pointed at Ma Liangcai and said, \"Him.\"","Pei Guanli followed the direction of his finger. The smile on her small face froze as she stammered, \"Chen Yi... he, he’s a bit old, but I guess it works...\"","Chen Yi smiled and shook his head. \"I’m not asking you to teach him, but his disciple—my grand-disciple.\" He pointed at Yuan Liu’er and added, \"That’s her.\"","Pei Guanli immediately breathed a sigh of relief. She sized up Yuan Liu’er and playfully agreed, \"Leave it to me.\"","\"Remember, only teach her the Pile Skill.\"","\"Alright... But Chen Yi, isn’t the Big Spear Pile Skill a bit too mediocre?\"","Chen Yi looked at her, raising an eyebrow. \"Do you have anything that isn’t mediocre?\"","Pei Guanli chuckled a few times and said sheepishly, \"My family does, but Ah Ma won’t let me pass it on to outsiders...\"","Chen Yi smiled and patted her forehead. \"The Big Spear Pile Skill will do just fine.\"","With Yuan Liu’er’s talent, even the most ordinary Pile Skill would be more than enough to temper her body in the Ninth Grade Realm. Not to mention she also had the Black Tortoise Concealment Technique...","After finishing with business, Chen Yi secretly instructed Pei Guanli a bit more, as he temporarily didn’t want Yuan Liu’er to know his true identity.","\"Don’t worry, Chen Yi! My lips are the tightest. Even Sister Jinghong hasn’t noticed...\"","Chen Yi offered a few words of praise upon hearing this, but he shook his head inwardly. Having this Tiger Girl deliver the letter to Xiao Jinghong that one time had been a move made out of sheer helplessness. Fortunately, he had made preparations in advance so as not to arouse Xiao Jinghong’s suspicion. Otherwise, he would have likely been exposed by now.","They chatted idly for a few more moments.","Chen Yi was just about to leave Pei Guanli alone at the Jishi Medicine Hall and head to the Hundred Herbs Hall by himself. Suddenly, a surge of Heaven and Earth’s Spiritual Mechanism welled up inside the Medicine Hall. A faint halo rippled outward like a wave, lasting for ten breaths before gradually dissipating.","Pei Guanli seemed to sense something and looked around suspiciously. \"Chen Yi, did someone just stir up Heaven and Earth’s Spiritual Mechanism here? Who is cultivating an Inner Power Heart Method or a Technique?\"","Chen Yi didn’t respond to her. Instead, he looked at Yuan Liu’er with mild surprise. At this moment, Yuan Liu’er was still standing beside Ma Liangcai. Her eyes were slightly closed, but her body was undergoing visible changes. Nourished and replenished by that surge of Heaven and Earth’s Spiritual Mechanism, her originally emaciated figure filled out slightly, and her complexion became much rosier.","Chen Yi naturally knew this was because Yuan Liu’er’s body was far too weak from suffering long-term starvation. If it were him, with a body tempered to the absolute limit by the Big Spear Pile Skill, Black Tortoise Concealment Technique, and Four Symbols Skill, the fluctuations of Heaven and Earth’s Spiritual Mechanism caused by a breakthrough in a Technique Realm would have almost no effect.","He muttered inwardly, \"But for her Medical Dao to reach the entry-level... how many days has it even been?\"","He couldn’t help but glance at Ma Liangcai, who remained completely oblivious to the anomaly, and his lips twitched slightly in disdain. For someone with such unparalleled talent to follow Ma Liangcai was a true waste of potential.","He thought, \"That dog. He’s studied the Medical Dao for so long and still hasn’t reached Minor Success. What an absolute blockhead.","\"Truly... a disgrace to the sect, an absolute disgrace.\"","Chen Yi shook his head inwardly. He gave Pei Guanli a few low-voiced instructions before getting up to leave.","Watching him walk away, Pei Guanli skipped over to Yuan Liu’er and scrutinized her carefully.","\"Chen Yi’s grand-disciple... Doesn’t that make me her martial grand-aunt?\" Pei Guanli murmured. Her eyes curved into crescent moons as she smiled, making Ma Liangcai, who had noticed her, feel a chill down his spine.","However, he knew Pei Guanli had been brought here by Chen Yi, so he tentatively spoke up. \"Miss, you...\"","Pei Guanli cast him a sideways glance. \"Call me Martial Aunt! What do you mean, ’Miss’?\"","Ma Liangcai was momentarily stunned before suddenly realizing what she meant. He solemnly stood up, bowed, and greeted, \"Martial Aunt. This disciple was impolite just now. Please forgive me, Martial Aunt.\"","Amused, Pei Guanli responded with a beaming smile. She then raised her chin, coughed lightly, and demanded, \"Speak. What business do you have with your martial aunt?\"","Ma Liangcai shook his head repeatedly, no longer daring to ask why she had been staring at Yuan Liu’er.","Pei Guanli waved her hand dismissively. \"If there’s nothing else, go back to your work. Don’t interrupt me from observing Chen Yi’s good grand-disciple.\"","\"Yes, yes, yes...\" Ma Liangcai breathed a sigh of relief and sat back down."]},{"number":608,"title":"Chapter 608 - 341: Junior Chen Yi Pays His Respects...","paragraphs":["\"It is my disciple’s blessing to have my martial aunt come and see her,\" he thought while treating a patient and glancing at Pei Guanli, who was staring unblinkingly at Yuan Liu’er.","About fifteen minutes later.","Yuan Liu’er woke up. Feeling incredibly refreshed, she instinctively stretched her body. Her bones and joints popped in unison, as if she had been reborn and received immense nourishment. However, before she had time to figure out why, she realized her situation and immediately apologized to Ma Liangcai.","\"Master, I... I fell asleep just now,\" she said apologetically.","Before Ma Liangcai could speak, Pei Guanli patted her shoulder and slung an arm around her. \"What do you mean, fell asleep? You’ve entered the entry-level of the Medical Dao and reaped the benefits.\"","Yuan Liu’er froze for a moment. Somewhat unaccustomed to the intimacy, she shrugged slightly, turned her head to look at her, and asked, \"Miss, are you saying I’ve reached the entry-level of the Medical Dao?\"","\"Yep, that’s what my brother-in-law said.\"","\"Brother-in-law?\"","\"Your martial grandfather. The shopkeeper of this medicine hall.\"","Ma Liangcai finally found a chance to interject. He stood up and said, \"Liu’er, why aren’t you greeting your martial grand-aunt?\"","Belatedly realizing the situation, Yuan Liu’er bowed. \"Liu’er greets Martial Grand-Aunt.\"","Pei Guanli’s smile grew even brighter, but noticing the other people in the medicine hall looking their way, she pulled Yuan Liu’er toward the inner hall. \"Come with me. Your martial grandfather asked me to tell you a few things before he left.\"","\"Oh...\"","Ma Liangcai sent them off with a smile. After wiping the cold sweat from his forehead, his face crumpled into a miserable expression. He had been teaching Yuan Liu’er the Medical Dao for no more than half a month in total, yet she had already reached the entry-level. His feelings were somewhat complicated.","\"Master was right. Liu’er’s talent is rare in this world. For me to be her mentor is truly, truly...\" Ma Liangcai couldn’t find the right word, mostly feeling that he was unworthy. After all, he had been studying under Chen Yi for so long, yet his Medical Dao had still not reached the Minor Success Realm.","\"Understand the constant to adapt to changes, understand the constant to adapt to changes... What does it mean to understand the constant to adapt to changes?\" he muttered.","Chen Yi naturally had no idea what was happening inside Jishi Medicine Hall. Even if he knew that the Tiger Girl was a bit unreliable, he couldn’t find anyone more suitable to teach Yuan Liu’er Martial Arts in his stead for now. Fortunately, after the Annual Examination, he would have more free time, so he didn’t have to worry about Pei Guanli leading Yuan Liu’er astray.","Chen Yi strolled along Chuandong Street, pausing every now and then. Just like when he came, he wasn’t in much of a hurry. He looked around as if on a spring outing, checking out this and that. He even bought a stick of candied haws and ate it with great relish.","The early afternoon sun shone brightly, accompanied by a cool breeze.","Everything along the way was vivid and clear. There were fewer commoners with sorrowful faces; Jianghu People laughed and cursed freely, street vendors called out warmly, and shop waiters shouted their slogans to attract customers. It was just like the first time Chen Yi came here—bustling, noisy, and with a faint hint of prosperity.","Of course, there were some changes. For instance, there were fewer Poshisu People on the streets, especially those leading barbarian slaves. After the incident with Asutai and Lv Jiunan, the Governor’s Office and the Prefectural Magistrate’s Office had arrested many Poshisu People. Some were convicted, while others were deported; all in all, it showed a newfound sense of caution. Even the City Guard Army, who normally wouldn’t patrol the streets during the day, were guarding the city’s main thoroughfares like government officials.","Chen Yi saw all this and couldn’t help but feel a sense of gratification.","Outsiders only knew that this was the Xiao Family’s doing—that it was the Xiao Family who eradicated Liu Hong and resolved the grain price crisis. However, as the instigator, Chen Yi couldn’t think that way. At the very least, he had to maintain the mindset of \"I have bled for the Xiao Family.\" That way, when Xiao Jinghong eventually found out what he had done, he would at least have some leverage to prevent her from dealing a heavy hand against him.","Chen Yi made his way to South Street. When his gaze swept over the Governor’s Office, he couldn’t help but chuckle.","Chen Yunfan was sitting boldly on the threshold, speaking to the crowd of commoners outside who were cursing Liu Hong and his accomplices. \"Save your breath. The man is dead. No matter how much you say, Lord Liu can’t hear you anyway, so why bother?","\"Or are you planning to follow him into the afterlife?\"","Unexpectedly, someone in the crowd shouted, \"You’re no good either!\"","Infuriated, Chen Yunfan scoffed and was about to march over to argue with the person, showing absolutely none of the dignity expected of a Junior Fourth-grade Assistant Governor.","After a bout of noisy arguing, the commoners gathered outside the office finally dispersed.","Having watched the whole spectacle, Chen Yi greeted Chen Yunfan from afar.","Chen Yunfan had naturally seen him early on. Seeing Chen Yi bow, he simply nodded and turned back into the Governor’s Office. He had just received a reward from the Holy Emperor that morning and had no desire to see Chen Yi right now. If he had to hear words like \"Congratulations,\" \"Felicitations,\" or \"Brother is brave and resourceful,\" he might just die of anger.","Chen Yi stared at his back for a moment in slight surprise but didn’t think much of it, assuming that they were just busy inside the Governor’s Office. Still, for Chen Yunfan to be this diligent was truly a rare sight.","\"It seems Chen Xuanji’s visit to Shu State is weighing heavily on Brother’s mind,\" Chen Yi muttered. Shaking his head, he headed straight for Hundred Herbs Hall.","He lacked any goodwill toward that \"father\" he had never met, and he had no idea if the man had any ulterior motives for coming to Shu State other than inspecting the Three Towns. Either way, he would cross that bridge when he came to it.","Not long after.","Chen Yi arrived outside the West Market and looked at the signboard hanging above the doors of Hundred Herbs Hall. The three characters he had written still shone brilliantly. Images flashed through his mind, illuminating his surroundings. Having not visited for several days, the exterior of Hundred Herbs Hall had also undergone a transformation.","Because Xinglin Hall had been shut down by the Government Office, Hundred Herbs Hall’s medicinal herb supply had returned to normal. They no longer needed to limit tea purchases, resulting in a continuous stream of customers.","There were also many scholars in long gowns gathered at the entrance, including quite a few elderly men. They sat clustered in a corner outside Hundred Herbs Hall, doing their best not to obstruct the passing pedestrians. Most of them had set up makeshift tables using wooden stools and were holding writing brushes, copying the calligraphy on the signboard.","Additionally, many travelers from out of town were pointing at the signboard.","\"As expected of Mr. Qingzhou, who is renowned throughout the world for his poetry and calligraphy. This new style—Cursive Script—is truly uninhibited and elegant,\" one traveler said.","\"You only see the surface, my friend. In truth, there are hidden profound mysteries in Mr. Qingzhou’s Calligraphy Dao,\" another traveler chimed in. \"Every stroke is free and unrestrained, but an underlying sense of aloof arrogance runs through it. Look closely at the character for ’Herb.’ Isn’t that downward stroke vigorous and powerful?\"","A middle-aged scholar stroked his beard and continued, \"When studying calligraphy, one must not only look at its form but also understand its intent.\"","\"You are absolutely right, my friend. We have been enlightened...\"","Chen Yi glanced at the scholars copying the signboard and was about to enter Hundred Herbs Hall to find Wang Ji and give him some instructions.","Unexpectedly, just as he lifted his foot, a cold, arrogant voice rang in his ear. \"Come, drink with me.\"","Chen Yi frowned slightly and turned to look at Yunqing Building behind him. Through a third-floor window facing the street, he saw a figure sitting with his back to the road. The man’s long black hair was tied with a red ribbon, and a glimpse of snow-white clothing could be seen on his shoulders.","\"It’s him?\" Chen Yi thought, his frown deepening as the man’s identity flashed through his mind. \"Why would he invite me for a drink?\"","The man was none other than the unfathomably powerful swordsman he had encountered after killing Du Cang with a punch.","—Monarch Xue Jian, Lone Immortal Ye.","Chen Yi just couldn’t understand why this man had sought him out.","After a moment of thought, Chen Yi looked around. Seeing that no one had noticed anything unusual, he turned and entered Yunqing Building.","He thanked the waiters inside, who were familiar with him, and went straight up to the third floor, arriving outside the private room. After straightening his clothes, he pushed the door open. Seeing Lone Immortal Ye sitting upright at the table, pouring and drinking wine by himself, Chen Yi turned and closed the door behind him.","CLICK.","Chen Yi took a seat at the table, sitting face-to-face with Lone Immortal Ye, and cupped his hands in greeting. \"Junior Chen Yi pays his respects to Monarch Xue Jian.\"","Lone Immortal Ye set down his wine cup, his long, narrow eyes fixing on Chen Yi with the sharpness of a drawn sword.","Chen Yi’s body tensed, but he forced himself to remain calm inward. With his current Cultivation, he was far inferior to Monarch Xue Jian. If Monarch Xue Jian wanted to kill him, even if he fought with his life on the line, he would likely end up dead.","Fortunately, Lone Immortal Ye only glanced at him before withdrawing his gaze. However, Heaven and Earth’s Spiritual Mechanism in their surroundings remained slightly unusual, as if forming a cage of Sword Intent, a world of its own.","As Lone Immortal Ye poured wine, he spoke seemingly to himself, \"It has only been a few days, yet your Sword Dao has reached Great Success...","\"Not bad.\""]},{"number":609,"title":"Chapter 609 - 342: Show You Some Respect!","paragraphs":["The private room echoed with the lingering sound. It was as empty as a desolate mountain forest; no sound from the outside world could be heard.","Chen Yi knew this was because Lone Immortal Ye’s Sword Dao had drawn in Heaven and Earth’s Spiritual Mechanism, confining it within the private room. It was much like the Black Magic Secret Skill used by \"Jackal\" Du Cang. People outside could not pry into anything happening in this room, nor could he hear or see anyone or anything beyond its walls.","Chen Yi sat upright at the table, looking straight at Lone Immortal Ye, meeting him with silence. After the incident with Immortal Bai, he didn’t believe his Black Tortoise Concealment Technique could hide him from Lone Immortal Ye. And the truth was, it couldn’t. However, Chen Yi couldn’t figure out why Lone Immortal Ye had specifically asked for him by name. Was it because of his rapid progress in Sword Dao? Or was it because of something else?","Chen Yi had no way of knowing. After some thought, he withdrew his gaze, grabbed the wine pot, poured a cup of wine, and said, \"Senior, please.\"","Without waiting for Lone Immortal Ye’s response, he downed it in one gulp. Since he was already here, he might as well make peace with it. Since he could neither hide nor fight his way out, responding to all changes by remaining unchanged was his only solution.","Lone Immortal Ye merely watched him coldly and indifferently, observing as he calmly poured the wine, drank it, and set down the cup.","Several breaths later, Lone Immortal Ye withdrew his gaze, picked up his own wine cup, and similarly downed it in one gulp.","The sharp Sword Intent filling the private room dissipated slightly. However, Lone Immortal Ye showed no intention of stopping. He poured and drank cup after cup, and soon, the pot of wine bottomed out.","Chen Yi stared at him blankly. \"The person who called me over for a drink is drinking alone in a sulk... Then why go through the trouble of inviting me here?\" he wondered. Chen Yi truly couldn’t understand this at all.","Seeing that Lone Immortal Ye had already broken the seal of a second jar of wine, Chen Yi felt somewhat helpless and followed suit, opening a jar himself. Only this time, he didn’t use the small wine cup. Instead, he grabbed an empty bowl, filled it to the brim, held it up to his chest with both hands, and said as usual, \"Senior, please.\"","Then, he chugged it in one breath. As the spicy Lang Wine slid down his throat, a warm current flowed into his chest and abdomen.","Chen Yi smacked his lips twice and, minding his own business, picked up his chopsticks and started eating the dishes. Crispy fried peanuts, cold sliced beef, hand-grabbed mutton... Chen Yi ate and drank, no longer overthinking Lone Immortal Ye’s intentions, focusing solely on filling his stomach.","Seeing his actions, Lone Immortal Ye put down the wine cup in his hand and surprisingly switched to a large bowl as well. He filled it with wine, tilted his head back, and swallowed it all in one gulp. After drinking, he mimicked Chen Yi and started eating the appetizers on the table.","Then came the second bowl, the third bowl... One jar, two jars, three jars...","Only half an hour passed, and Chen Yi and Lone Immortal Ye had finished all six jars of wine in the private room. Neither of them used True Essence to dissipate the alcohol. With three jars of wine in their stomachs, their faces had turned liver-red.","Lone Immortal Ye shook his wine jar. Only a few drops of wine fell into his bowl. A frown appeared on his usually expressionless face. He looked over at Chen Yi’s hand—where the last half-pot of Lang Wine remained. \"Bring it here.\"","Chen Yi gripped the wine pot but did not hand it over. He gently breathed out a puff of alcohol-laced air and, emboldened by the liquor, asked, \"Did you summon me this time, Senior, just to... drink?\"","Lone Immortal Ye shot him a glance, his gaze then landing on the pot of wine. He gently raised a finger.","The surrounding Heaven and Earth’s Spiritual Mechanism instantly pressed down on Chen Yi like Da Shan. Caught off guard, Chen Yi’s figure sank. He was almost crushed by this majestic and vast heaviness formed by Heaven and Earth’s Spiritual Mechanism.","He abruptly gritted his teeth. His Martial Arts of the Punch, spear, Blade, sword, Step, and body completely erupted. Even so, within this cage-like private room, he only managed to snatch a sliver of Heaven and Earth’s Spiritual Mechanism. But for Chen Yi, this tiny bit was enough.","His fingers gripping the wine pot twitched slightly. Following a series of CRACKING sounds, the porcelain wine pot was covered in spiderweb cracks. If he used even a fraction more strength, the wine pot would inevitably shatter.","Chen Yi stared at Lone Immortal Ye, forcing out a smile. \"Senior, this wine is mine.\" He wanted to use this method to tell Lone Immortal Ye, \"I respect you, but don’t push your luck.\"","Lone Immortal Ye naturally saw through his intentions. Looking at the porcelain pot that was slowly leaking wine, he raised his hand and dispersed Heaven and Earth’s Spiritual Mechanism.","Chen Yi’s Heart Spirit relaxed slightly. Fortunately, Tiger Girl had previously told him some things about Lone Immortal Ye, allowing him to determine that Lone Immortal Ye was not a bloodthirsty person. After all, if he was truly bloodthirsty and cruel, given that level of hatred, why wouldn’t he have slaughtered the entire Le family?","Chen Yi’s hand gripping the wine pot loosened slightly. He took the opportunity to pour a cup of wine for each of them and said, \"Senior Sword Monarch, please.\"","Lone Immortal Ye glanced at his hand, then at the wine cup in front of him. The flush on his face faded bit by bit, and his eyes became increasingly clear. He clearly didn’t plan on continuing to drink.","\"Gongye Bai said that before sparring with me, there needs to be a match between the younger generation.","\"His candidate is a member of the Wind and Rain Tower.\"","Seeing Lone Immortal Ye staring straight at him, Chen Yi caught sight of the wine cup by his hand from the corner of his eye and secretly curled his lip. \"To think he actually despises the fact that the cup of wine was touched by my hand. Just because his title contains the word ’Snow’, does he think he’s pure and pristine?\" he thought.","Thinking this, Chen Yi finished the wine in his cup and pretended not to understand as he said, \"The Wind and Rain Tower, huh? Their reputation precedes them.","\"I’m guessing the person Senior Immortal Bai chose should be his disciple, Shui Hetong, right?","\"That is quite a formidable figure. I have long heard of his name. They say his aptitude is extraordinary. Not only did he inherit Immortal Bai’s legacy, but he also achieved mastery through comprehensive study, carving out his own path of the Punch.\"","After spinning this half-truth, Chen Yi looked at Lone Immortal Ye and asked seriously, \"I wonder who you have chosen, Senior? They must be a peerless genius as well, right?\"","Lone Immortal Ye stared at him and spat out one word: \"You.\"","\"Me?\" Chen Yi pointed at himself and said with a smile, \"Senior must be joking. My Cultivation is insufficient, and my Technique Realm is low. How could I possibly be a match for that Shui Hetong?\""]},{"number":610,"title":"Chapter 610 - 342: Show You Some Respect!","paragraphs":["He knew nothing good would come from this man seeking him out. So this was his plan.","Asking him to duel the rising martial arts star chosen by Immortal Bai... Did he have too much free time on his hands or what?","Lone Immortal Ye seemed to have anticipated his response. \"Gongye Bai told me to choose you,\" he said coldly. \"He also said that as long as I said three words to you, you would agree.\"","\"Oh?\"","\"Xiao Jinghong.\"","Chen Yi’s smile froze as he crushed the wine jug in his hand to pieces.","He stared at Lone Immortal Ye for a long time before flashing a smile again. \"Since you think so highly of me, Senior, I suppose I’ll give it a try.","\"However, you also know my current Cultivation, Senior. I am truly no match for Shui Hetong. If I lose, you can’t blame me for not trying my best.\"","Damn it. Immortal Bai and Lone Immortal Ye, those two shameless old geezers, actually threatened him. They completely lacked the demeanor of senior experts.","Lone Immortal Ye seemed to guess his thoughts, the flush on his face fading a fraction. \"If you win, I can promise to do one thing for you.\"","Chen Yi raised an eyebrow. \"Anything at all?\"","\"Yes.\"","\"Go to the Le family and... Senior, don’t get angry, I’m just joking.\"","Seeing a sword blade suddenly hovering right between his eyebrows, Chen Yi let out a dry laugh and added, \"I will definitely give this matter my all.\"","Rumor had it that Shui Hetong’s Cultivation had already entered the Upper Three Grades. His Fist Dao Realm was quite high, possessing the momentum of \"a punch that could topple a thousand miles of mountains and rivers.\"","Moreover, as a disciple of Immortal Bai, the skills he had learned couldn’t possibly be weak.","His strength was definitely greater, not weaker, than that of \"Jackal\" Du Cang and Yan Jingchen.","Chen Yi naturally wasn’t confident.","But thinking it over carefully, he figured he could give it a try.","A promise from a figure like Lone Immortal Ye carried the weight of ten thousand mountains. If used well, it could act as a surprise force capable of holding off a massive army.","Because of this, Chen Yi’s resistance weakened a bit.","Seeing him agree, Lone Immortal Ye’s lips moved slightly as if he were speaking to someone. Shortly after, a waiter from the Yunqing Building walked in carrying six jugs of wine. He respectfully arranged them neatly before backing out of the room.","Chen Yi looked at the liquor, then at Lone Immortal Ye, whose complexion had returned to normal. Circulating the True Essence within his body, he neutralized the alcohol in his stomach.","Lone Immortal Ye paid no attention to his actions. Just like before, he slapped open the paper seal on a wine jug and drank.","Chen Yi had no choice but to risk his life and keep the gentleman company.","After three rounds of drinks.","After finishing his second jug of wine, Lone Immortal Ye suddenly looked at him and said, \"Your talent is the greatest I have ever seen in my life.\"","Chen Yi slapped open his third jug of Lang Wine and smiled. \"You flatter me, Senior. I just have somewhat better luck, that’s all.\"","Lone Immortal Ye shook his head slightly. \"Human strength has its limits. Even someone as powerful as Gongye Bai has only cultivated three Daos.","\"As for me, only my Sword Dao and Step Dao have entered the Extreme Realm.","\"In your Martial Arts, you have made remarkable achievements in body, step, punch, spear, blade, and sword. This is exceptionally rare in this world.\"","Seeing him praise him endlessly, Chen Yi wasn’t pleased. Instead, he grew a little wary and guarded.","\"Senior... do you have further instructions?\"","Surprisingly, Lone Immortal Ye nodded directly. His tone softened slightly, shifting from cold to plain. \"In two years, there will be an event called Debating and Striving for the Lead on the South Sea. If any of your Daos reaches the Extreme Realm, you may also go and take a look.\"","\"Debating and Striving for the Lead?\"","\"Yes. People from Great Wei, the Barbarian Race, Poshisu Country, and even Japan will go.\"","Chen Yi’s expression shifted slightly. He looked at him and asked carefully, \"Will they all be senior experts at the same Realm as you and Immortal Bai?\"","Lone Immortal Ye gave a slight nod and said, \"Gongye Bai, myself, and Nun Jingci from Wumeng Mountain.\"","\"Nun Jingci? Is her strength comparable to yours as well?\"","Chen Yi had naturally heard of Nun Jingci’s name. Previously, Xiao Wan’er would travel to Wumeng Mountain every September and October to recuperate her health, all with the help of this Nun Jingci.","However, he had only assumed that Nun Jingci specialized in the Medical Dao. He never expected her to be an expert on par with Lone Immortal Ye and Immortal Bai.","Seeing Lone Immortal Ye nod, Chen Yi said thoughtfully, \"No wonder Immortal Bai came to Shu State. He’s here to invite Nun Jingci.\"","He looked at Lone Immortal Ye and added, \"Is your duel with Senior Immortal Bai also because of this Debating and Striving for the Lead on the South Sea?\"","Lone Immortal Ye nodded once again. \"Worthy opponents are hard to find. My hands were itching for a fight.\" Pausing for a moment, he then shook his head and said, \"Gongye Bai didn’t just come to Shu State for invitations and spars. He has other matters to attend to.\"","Chen Yi perked up his ears, wanting to hear the details, but he waited and waited without any follow-up. He couldn’t help but feel a bit exasperated.","Fortunately, he wasn’t overly curious, otherwise hearing only half a sentence would have driven him crazy.","\"May I ask what exactly is this Debating and Striving for the Lead? Why does Senior Immortal Bai have to invite people personally?\"","Lone Immortal Ye continued to shake his head, saying, \"It cannot be spoken of.\"","\"...\"","Chen Yi cursed inwardly, guessing it was probably because his current Cultivation and Techniques were still insufficient. So, he didn’t ask any further.","Then, he lifted his wine jug and gestured toward Lone Immortal Ye. \"Please.\"","Lone Immortal Ye was straightforward, replying with a single word. \"Come.\"","It wasn’t until the sun set in the evening that the two finally finished their battle.","The result was naturally a tie, with each of them downing ten jugs of wine.","Even with their Martial Arts to support them and the ability to use True Essence to neutralize the alcohol, they both felt somewhat tipsy by this point.","Chen Yi checked the sky outside the window, stood up, and cupped his hands. \"Thank you for your hospitality, Senior. I have other matters to attend to, so I’ll be taking my leave first.\"","Lone Immortal Ye gave him a glance. Resting his hand on the hilt of his sword, his entire body transformed into a streak of light. In the blink of an eye, he vanished into the horizon.","Chen Yi was stunned. His mouth gaped slightly as he stared at the spot where the man had disappeared, standing frozen for a long time.","\"Goddamn it...\"","No matter how good-tempered Chen Yi was, encountering such a senior expert left him speechless for a moment. He could only curse inwardly. There was nothing he could do. Lone Immortal Ye had run off, which meant someone had to pay the silver for the food and liquor in this private room.","Shaking his head with a sigh, Chen Yi stumbled out of the private room and headed downstairs to the counter to settle the bill.","\"Mr. Qingzhou, twenty jugs of top-quality Lang Wine comes to one hundred taels of silver. As for the food, consider it complimentary snacks to go with your drinks.\"","Expressionless, Chen Yi pulled out his coin pouch, slapped down a silver note, and turned to leave the Yunqing Building, walking toward the Hundred Herbs Hall across the street.","He had to commit this debt to memory—on the twenty-ninth day of September in the 21st year of Anhe, \"Monarch Xue Jian,\" Lone Immortal Ye, owed him a hundred taels of silver!","Floating in the sky atop his long sword, Lone Immortal Ye looked down at Chen Yi entering the Hundred Herbs Hall. A rare trace of a smile appeared on his icy face.","\"Not a bad tolerance for liquor...\" Immediately after, he turned into a streak of light and departed.","***","Thanks to the unexpected disruption caused by Lone Immortal Ye, Chen Yi’s leisurely mood was completely ruined.","After arriving at the Quiet Chamber of the Hundred Herbs Hall, he had Wang Ji bring him pen and paper, then wrote down his arrangements one by one.","\"Medicine supply: Head to the Mountain Race as soon as possible. If they ask, give them Pei Guanli’s name.","\"Expansion into Shu State must not be delayed. Using Guangyuan and the Prefecture City as our foundation, spread out to the surrounding areas. Strive to cover all of Shu State before the end of the year.","\"Additionally, buy the five Xinglin Hall shops here in the Prefecture City. There’s no need to limit the tea supply...\"","After writing down all the tasks one by one, Chen Yi naturally spoke about other unrelated matters aloud. He inquired about the recent situation of the Hundred Herbs Hall, asked how many silver coins the Medicine Hall was distributing as profits, and questioned the whereabouts of Mr. Chen Yu, the owner, among other things.","Wang Ji smiled and answered as he read the contents on the paper.","Once the official business was concluded, Chen Yi noticed it was getting late. He thought for a moment and asked, \"Are Guard Liu and Zhang Dabao not here?\"","\"They’re currently staying with the guards from the Celestial Sect,\" Wang Ji replied. \"Following the boss’s instructions, since the expansion of the Hundred Herbs Hall concerns the Marquis’s Mansion, Guard Liu was tasked with teaching Martial Arts to the other guards.\"","Chen Yi raised an eyebrow slightly and mouthed wordlessly, \"Liu Lang’s idea?\"","Unexpectedly, Wang Ji shook his head. \"It was the Celestial Sect disciples who requested it themselves.","\"I’m not too clear on the details, but I heard that the previous attack by the Five Poison Sect made them lose face. They all want to improve their Cultivation as quickly as possible.","\"So Xue Duanyun sought out Liu Lang and asked him to help instruct the others.\"","Chen Yi nodded in understanding, a hint of a smile appearing on his lips. \"Liu Lang has finally done something productive.\"","After chatting for a bit longer, Chen Yi gave Wang Ji a few more instructions before getting up to leave.","He didn’t forget to first stop by the Jishi Medicine Hall to pick up Pei Guanli, bringing her along with him back to the Xiao family.","However, for some unknown reason, Tiger Girl was rather depressed and unusually quiet along the way.","Although Chen Yi wasn’t in the best of moods either, he was free-spirited by nature. If there was a problem, he would simply find a way to solve it. Thus, he smiled and asked, \"How are you getting along with Liu’er?\"","Pei Guanli snapped out of her daze and looked at him with confusion on her face. \"Chen Yi, is my talent in Martial Arts very poor?\"","Chen Yi couldn’t help but laugh, finally understanding the reason behind her gloomy mood.","\"Of course you’re not.\"","But that also depended on who she was comparing herself to..."]},{"number":611,"title":"Chapter 611 - 343: This Inspires the Most Yearning","paragraphs":["It was no wonder Pei Guanli was in a bad mood.","Anyone would feel frustrated watching someone who had just taken up the Pile Skill make such rapid, visible progress in their Cultivation.","Pei Guanli sighed heavily. \"Sister Liu’er actually took less than a quarter of an hour to generate Qi Mechanism and temper her muscles, bones, and flesh.\"","She looked at Chen Yi, pouting. \"Brother-in-law, did you know all along that her talent in Martial Arts was extraordinary?\"","Chen Yi nodded. \"Liu’er’s talent is indeed extraordinary.\"","However, even he hadn’t expected Yuan Liu’er to take such a short amount of time to practice the Pile Skill. Even when he first practiced the Big Spear Pile Skill, it had taken him the better part of an hour to gain Initial Insight. This alone was proof of just how high Yuan Liu’er’s Martial Arts talent truly was.","Pei Guanli sulked. Putting on an old and wise act, she clasped her hands behind her back and sighed. \"Every generation of the Jianghu produces its own talents. The new waves will inevitably crush the old.\"","Chen Yi smiled and tapped her forehead, stifling her heavy sighs.","\"Weren’t you just saying at noon that you were going to work hard on your Cultivation to break through to the Seventh Grade Realm as soon as possible? Why are you losing steam now?","\"Instead of spouting this nonsense, you’d be better off going back and focusing on your Cultivation. Perhaps in a few days, you’ll make a breakthrough.\"","Pei Guanli rubbed her forehead and pursed her lips. \"It’s all your fault...\"","She knew Chen Yi wouldn’t accept a disciple for no reason, especially someone like Ma Liangcai. It must have all been for the highly talented Yuan Liu’er.","Fortunately, Pei Guanli was broad-minded. She quickly tossed her frustration aside. Her eyes darting around, she said, \"Brother-in-law, after the Annual Examination, are you going to teach Liu’er personally?\"","Chen Yi looked around and gave a slight nod. \"Her talent in Calligraphy Dao is equally impressive.\"","Pei Guanli naturally knew he was trying to avoid suspicion, but she didn’t mind. Chuckling, she asked, \"Then will you bring me along too?\"","\"You?\"","\"Yeah.\"","Seeing that she wasn’t joking, Chen Yi thought for a moment before nodding. \"Your handwriting is indeed a bit lacking. You can join Liu’er when the time comes.\"","Pei Guanli was just about to nod happily when she suddenly realized his meaning. \"You... Brother-in-law, are you saying that besides...\"","She threw a few mock punches and kicks, then mimed writing. \"I have to do that too?\"","Chen Yi gave her a sidelong glance. \"What do you think?\"","Pei Guanli’s face fell. \"Reading is my least favorite thing... Can I skip the writing?\"","\"What do you think?\"","\"No, right? Ugh, fine, I’ll write.\"","\"Mm...\"","The two chatted and laughed all the way back to the Xiao Family.","The afterglow of the setting sun lingered, casting a dreamy, ethereal glow of evening clouds that stretched their shadows long. Although the pedestrians on the road were in a hurry, many still cast sidelong glances at Chen Yi and Pei Guanli.","The former now had quite the reputation in Shu State City.","Not only did scholars recognize him, but even the commoners in the streets and alleys had heard the name \"Mr. Qingzhou.\" To this day, storytellers in teahouses and entertainment quarters were still recounting how \"Song of the Water Melody: Mid-Autumn\" took first place at the poetry gathering.","And after Chen Yi’s Poetry and Calligraphy Dao spread across the Nine State and Three Prefectures, people would occasionally arrive in Shu State, bringing rumors from the outside world.","One prominent scholar praised \"Song of the Water Melody: When Will the Bright Moon Appear?\" as the greatest Mid-Autumn poem in history, claiming that future generations would be hard-pressed to surpass it. Or a famous calligrapher who had the privilege of viewing Chen Yi’s Cursive Script copybooks was absolutely astounded and began tirelessly imitating and studying it.","Even from the Capital Prefecture, a few snippets of praise trickled in: \"Chen Qingzhou’s mastery of Cursive Script is no less significant to the Calligraphy Dao than the teachings of the ancient sages.\"","The one who spoke these words was none other than Wei Chi, also known as Wei Cixin, one of the Two Sages of Calligraphy Dao in the Great Wei Dynasty. Not only was he a member of the Royal Family, but he was also the dean of the Imperial Academy in the Capital Prefecture. Consequently, the name \"Chen Qingzhou\" became widely known, especially among scholars devoted to Calligraphy Dao.","It wasn’t hard to understand why. His mastery of Cursive Script pioneered a new path in the Great Wei, allowing more people obsessed with Calligraphy Dao to try and forge their own paths, no longer limited to Wei Qing’s Style.","As for Pei Guanli... The Mountain Race girl was an independent spirit. Her attire and behavior made it hard not to attract the attention of outsiders.","Of course, most commoners in Shu State feared the people of the Mountain Race. It wasn’t surprising. Everyone was afraid of Witchcraft, Poisonous Insects, and Poisonous Gu.","A short while later.","Chen Yi and Pei Guanli returned to the Xiao Family. They quieted their footsteps and subtly crossed the front courtyard.","As soon as they reached the middle courtyard, Chen Yi caught sight of the Armored Warriors guarding outside the Qingjing Residence. He thought to himself that something must have happened. No wonder he hadn’t seen Wang Lixing, Liu Si’er, or the others in the front courtyard.","Seeing the two of them, Wang Lixing cupped his fists in a salute. \"Second Son-in-law, Miss Pei.\"","Chen Yi smiled in greeting and asked casually, \"Do we have guests in the estate?\"","Feeling no need to hide it, Wang Lixing lowered his voice. \"Duke Qian brought men to deliver grain to the Marquis.\"","He thought, \"Duke Qian, Zhang Xuan? That shameless old man?\"","Chen Yi nodded in understanding and smiled. \"No wonder there’s such a big commotion in the estate.\"","He had originally thought it was Xiao Jinghong returning to the Xiao Family after hearing about the imperial decree. He certainly hadn’t expected Zhang Xuan to come in person.","After exchanging a few more words, Chen Yi brought Pei Guanli back to the Spring Lotus Garden.","In the pavilion, Xiaodie was keeping Xiao Wuge, who had changed into dry clothes, company as they chatted and laughed.","Pei Guanli’s eyes darted playfully. She pushed her tender white feet off the bluestone slabs and shouted with a laugh, \"Watch out!\"","The Bell chimed with a JINGLE.","Hearing the sound, Xiao Wuge turned his head, only to see a small fist enlarging before his eyes. He hastily ducked and nimbly dodged the blow.","Pei Guanli was somewhat surprised. Even though she had held back ninety percent of her strength, her speed was still much higher than that of a Lower Ninth Grade Cultivator.","\"Xiao Wuge, your Martial Arts are improving really fast, even if you still can’t compare to a certain monster.\"","Xiao Wuge finally saw who it was, his tense expression turning to joy. \"Sister Pei, you’re back.\"","Pei Guanli placed a hand on her hip and reached out to poke his forehead, giggling. \"If I hadn’t come back soon, your Martial Arts would’ve surpassed mine, Xiao Wuge.\""]}]);
